From 888222e6f95e3e36d1b94f263339a25bdd88b317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:35:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the direct GnuPG verification with %openpgpverify, which
uses Sequoia sqv, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Refresh gpgkey-B56B8B9D9915AA8796EDC013DFFF2CDB19FC338D.gpg from
keyservers/WKD: same certificate(s), with self-signatures our copy was
missing; the commands are in the spec comment.
Release bumped with a changelog entry.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 ...6B8B9D9915AA8796EDC013DFFF2CDB19FC338D.gpg | Bin 5659 -> 5827 bytes
 libHX.spec                                    |  12 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

